{
  "answer_markdown": "To ensure your requests are processed in the EU, you should use the [`api.eu.mistral.ai`](https://api.eu.mistral.ai) endpoint. This endpoint is explicitly designed for inference processing within the European Union and includes multiple data centers in EU and EFTA countries, albeit with a regional upcharge. The global endpoint [`api.mistral.ai`](https://api.mistral.ai), on the other hand, does not commit to a specific inference location [1].\n\nBy switching to `api.eu.mistral.ai`, you gain the benefit of data processing within the EU, which may be necessary for compliance with regional data laws or privacy regulations. However, you will incur a regional upcharge, and you may experience slightly different performance or availability characteristics compared to the global endpoint. Additionally, some advanced features or tiers (like the Priority Tier) may be subject to regional capacity and limitations, depending on the account setup and model availability [3].\n\nThere is no mention of specific features or capabilities lost when using `api.eu.mistral.ai` compared to the global endpoint. The main difference is the geographic location of processing and the associated upcharge [1].",
  "citations": [
