{
  "answer_markdown": "The `safe_prompt` parameter is a deprecated boolean flag that, when set to `true`, prepends a system prompt to your messages for moderation against sensitive content such as harmful, unethical, prejudiced, or negative content. This system prompt is designed to ensure replies are respectful and safe [1][2].\n\n### Example of Using `safe_prompt` in TypeScript\n```typescript\nconst chatResponse = await client.chat.complete(\n    model: 'mistral-large-latest',\n    messages: [{role: 'user', content: 'What is the best French cheese?'}],\n    safePrompt: true\n);\n```\n\nThe server rejects the `safe_prompt` flag because it is deprecated and should not be used. The documentation explicitly states that `safe_prompt` is deprecated and recommends using [Custom Guardrails](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/safety-moderation#custom-guardrails) instead, which provides more control over moderation categories and thresholds directly in your API requests [1].\n\nSince `safe_prompt` is no longer part of the request, you should remove it and replace it with the recommended Custom Guardrails approach.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Safe Prompt is deprecated. We recommend using Custom Guardrails instead, which provides more control over moderation categories and thresholds directly in your API requests."
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Toggling the safe prompt will prepend your messages with the following system prompt:"
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

