  "answer_markdown": "Yes, there is a REST API endpoint you can call from any language to manage handoffs and the Agents beta. The [REST API](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/connectors/confirmation#raw-api) allows you to manage conversation IDs and tool call IDs yourself, unlike the Python SDK which uses `RunContext` and `DeferredToolCallsException`.

Here is the cURL example for creating an agent (which can be used in handoffs) from the sources:

```bash
curl --location "https://api.mistral.ai/v1/agents" \
     --header 'Content-Type: application/json' \
     --header 'Accept: application/json' \
     --header "Authorization: Bearer $MISTRAL_API_KEY" \
     --data '{
     "model": "mistral-large-latest",
     "name": "finance-agent",
     "description": "Agent used to answer financial related requests"
  }'
```

This endpoint is documented under [operation-agents_api_v1_agents_create](https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/beta/agents#operation-agents_api_v1_agents_create) and is part of the beta Agents API [3].

Additionally, the [Handoffs](https://docs.mistral.ai/studio/agents/handoffs) feature supports chaining multiple agents and tools, and the REST API is explicitly mentioned as a way to implement confirmation flows without relying on the Python SDK [1].",
