  "answer_markdown": "The API returns the following rate-limit headers on a chat completion:\n\n- `X-RateLimit-Remaining`: Indicates the remaining number of requests or tokens before the limit is hit. This header helps monitor usage before reaching the limit.\n\nThe numbers behind the rate-limit headers come from the following:\n\n1. **Requests per second**: This is the request throughput limit for the model, enforced independently of token limits. It varies by subscription tier and model, and can be checked in the [limits page](https://admin.mistral.ai/plateforme/limits) [2].\n2. **Tokens per minute**: This is the token throughput limit for the model. It also varies by subscription tier and model, and is enforced independently of request limits. It can also be checked in the [limits page](https://admin.mistral.ai/plateforme/limits) [2].\n\nIf these limits are exceeded, the API returns a `429 Too Many Requests` response [2].\n\n[2]: https://docs.mistral.ai/resources/known-limitations#rate-limits",
