{
  "answer_markdown": "Mistral does not provide an official SDK for server-side Dart. However, a community-maintained third-party SDK is available: [mistralai_client_dart](https://github.com/nomtek/mistralai_client_dart) [2].\n\nIf you choose to hand-roll HTTP, you would typically use the REST API directly. Below is an example of a `POST /v1/client/sessions` request for minting a token (used for authentication), but for general model inference, you would call the appropriate endpoint (e.g., `/v1/completions` or `/v1/chat`).\n\n```bash\ncurl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/client/sessions \\\n  -X POST \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $MISTRAL_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"purpose\": \"realtime\",\n    \"model\": \"voxtral-mini-transcribe-realtime-2602\"\n  }'\n```\n\nThe official documentation does not provide Dart-specific REST API examples, so you would need to reference Mistral's general API documentation for the exact structure of other endpoints [3].\n\n**Note**: The third-party SDK is not actively maintained or supported by Mistral AI, so use it with caution [2].",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "Please note that these clients are not actively maintained or supported by Mistral AI."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "quote": "Call `POST /v1/client/sessions` from your backend with your API key."
    }
  ],
