message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "The Vibe CLI reads `config.toml` from the following locations, in this order of precedence:\n\n1. Project-level: `./.vibe/config.toml` in the current working directory.\n2. User-level: `~/.vibe/config.toml` in your home directory.\n\nWhen both a project-level and a user-level `config.toml` exist, the project-level configuration takes precedence over the user-level one, but only if the working directory is trusted. Otherwise, only the user-level configuration is used.[1]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "The CLI looks for `config.toml` in this order:\n1. `./.vibe/config.toml` in the current working directory (project-level).\n2. `~/.vibe/config.toml` in your home directory (user-level).\n\nProject-level configuration takes precedence over user-level configuration. Project configuration is loaded only when the working directory is trusted."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

