  "answer_markdown": "The Vibe CLI runs built-in commands with `/` (e.g., `/model`, `/help`, `/config`) and shell commands with `!` (e.g., `!ls -l`). It does not run these commands without asking unless the active agent is in `auto-approve` mode, which auto-approves every tool execution, including shell commands.\n\nTo add your own slash commands, you can create a skill with `user-invocable: true` in the frontmatter. The skill name will then become available with `/skill-name` autocompletion in the CLI prompt.\n\nHere is the code snippet from the sources to add a custom slash command:\n\n```text\n> /model\n```",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "Type `/` to open the slash-command picker with autocompletion. Use it for built-in commands like `/help`, `/model`, `/config`"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "To run a shell command directly from the CLI, prefix it with `!`. For example: `!ls` or `!git status`."
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "quote": "The `auto-approve` agent auto-approves every tool execution, including shell commands."
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "quote": "Set `user-invocable: true` in the frontmatter and the skill name becomes available with `/skill-name` autocompletion in the CLI prompt"
