message.content:
{
  "answer_markdown": "The Vibe CLI loads **up to two `AGENTS.md` files** from the following locations:\n\n1. **User-level**: `~/.vibe/AGENTS.md` (or in `$VIBE_HOME` if set).\n2. **Project-level**: The first `AGENTS.md` found while walking up parent directories from the current working directory, but only if the location is a **trusted folder** [2].\n\n**Example**:\n```text\n/\n  dir_1/\n    AGENTS.md      <- never loaded: location is not trusted\n    dir_2/         <- trusted\n      AGENTS.md\n      dir_3/\n        AGENTS.md  <- loaded\n        project/   <- cwd (no AGENTS.md here)\n```\n\n**Note**:\n- Trusted folders are defined in `~/.vibe/trusted_folders.toml` [4].\n- The CLI auto-discovers `AGENTS.md` files in sub-directories [2].\n- Project-level `AGENTS.md` is ignored unless the directory is trusted [6].\n",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "The CLI loads up to two `AGENTS.md` files into context to follow project-specific agent instructions"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "1. **User-level**: `~/.vibe/AGENTS.md` (or in `$VIBE_HOME` if you set it)."
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "quote": "2. **Project-level**: starting from the current working directory and walking up parent directories (but only inside [trusted folders](https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/code/safety-approvals-permissions#trusted-folders)), the first `AGENTS.md` found is loaded."
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "quote": "A project can ship its own Vibe configuration (like agents, skills, MCP servers, and tool permissions) in a `.vibe/` directory at the repository root."
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "quote": "The CLI checks whether the current working directory is trusted before loading project-level configuration, skills, or agent files."
    }
  ],
  "insufficient_evidence": false
}

