{
  "answer_markdown": "The supported transports for an MCP server with the Vibe CLI are:\n\n- `http`: when the server is reachable over standard HTTP.\n\n- `streamable-http`: when the server is reachable over HTTP and supports streaming responses.\n\n- `stdio`: when the server is a local process started from a command.\n\nMCP tools are named using the pattern `{server_name}_{tool_name}`. For example, a tool named `get` from a server called `fetch_server` would be accessed as `fetch_server_get`.\n\nTo configure permissions for MCP tools, you can use the `[tools.<tool_name>]` block in the configuration. For instance:\n\n```toml\n[tools.fetch_server_get]\npermission = \"always\"\n```\n\nPermissions can be set to `always` to auto-allow the tool or `ask` to prompt before use. Additionally, you can restrict which MCP tools are active using `enabled_tools` and `disabled_tools` with filters like exact names, glob patterns, or regex.\n\nExample:\n\n```toml\n# Only enable serena's tools\nenabled_tools = [\"serena_*\"]\n\n# Disable all MCP tools and grep\ndisabled_tools = [\"mcp_*\", \"grep\"]\n```",
  "citations": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "MCP servers extend the Vibe Code CLI with external tools through the Model Context Protocol."
    },
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "the CLI does not yet support MCP servers that require OAuth authentication."
    },
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "the server is reachable over standard HTTP."
    },
    {
      "n": 1,
      "quote": "the server is reachable over HTTP and supports streaming responses."
    },
