parsed.answer_markdown:
The model `mistral-small-latest` accepts a `document_url` inside a chat message, as shown in the cURL example under Document QnA > Document AI QnA > Usage > Leverage Document QnA [1].

However, the `document_url` inside a chat message is not the same as the OCR endpoint. The OCR endpoint uses a different request structure, where `document_url` is part of a `document` object in the request body, and it is used to extract text, images, and metadata from documents [2].

In the OCR endpoint, the `document_url` can be part of a `DocumentURLChunk` under the `document` field, and it supports additional parameters like `pages`, `include_image_base64`, and more for structured output [2].

The chat message example uses a simpler structure where `document_url` is directly provided within a chat message content array [1].

```bash
curl https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer ${MISTRAL_API_KEY}" \
  -d '{
    "model": "mistral-small-latest",
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "what is the last sentence in the document"
          },
          {
            "type": "document_url",
            "document_url": "data:application/pdf;base64,<base64_pdf>"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }'
```

